=== Side Ratio Proof Diagram ===
This auxiliary construction extends a standard <imath>30^\circ</imath>-<imath>60^\circ</imath>-<imath>90^\circ</imath> right triangle (<imath>\triangle XYZ</imath>) to create a larger <imath>15^\circ</imath>-<imath>75^\circ</imath>-<imath>90^\circ</imath> right triangle (<imath>\triangle XYW</imath>). This layout allows calculation of the side ratios without using trigonometry functions:

<asy>
import geometry;
size(8cm);

// Coordinates (Scaled up slightly for layout clarity)
pair X = (0,0);
pair Y = (0,2);
pair Z = (2*sqrt(3),0);
pair W = (2*sqrt(3) + 4, 0); // Extending base segment by length of hypotenuse (4 units)

// Draw triangles with clear, solid lines
draw(X--Y--W--cycle, linewidth(1.2pt));
draw(Y--Z, linewidth(1.2pt));

// Primary Vertex Labels
label("$X$", X, SW);
label("$Y$", Y, NW);
label("$Z$", Z, S);
label("$W$", W, SE);

// Clear Side Length Numbers
label("$1$", (X+Y)/2, W);
label("$\sqrt{3}$", (X+Z)/2, S);
label("$2$", (Y+Z)/2, NE);
label("$2$", (Z+W)/2, S);

// Clear Angle Degree Measures (Placed neatly inside/around corners)
label("$60^\circ$", Y, 2.5*SE);
label("$30^\circ$", Z, 2*NW);
label("$15^\circ$", W, 4.5*W);
label("$75^\circ$", Y, 2.5*S);

// Structural Right Angle Marker at X
draw(rightanglemark(Y,X,W,3mm));

// Explanation of construction
// Since segment ZW = YZ = 2, triangle YZW is an isosceles triangle. 
// The exterior angle at Z is 30 degrees, making internal angles ZYW = ZWY = 15 degrees.
// Therefore, the larger right triangle XYW has angles 15-75-90.
// Shorter leg / Longer leg = XY / XW = 1 / (2 + sqrt(3)).
// Rationalizing the denominator: 1 / (2 + sqrt(3)) * (2 - sqrt(3)) / (2 - sqrt(3)) = 2 - sqrt(3).
</asy>

